n Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6452f67ccada8c80a213b32735fb106e5b65d3ae.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6452f67ccada8c80a213b32735fb106e5b65d3ae.001.1"},{"event":"Winter Storm Warning","headline":"Winter Storm Warning issued November 1 at 10:57AM MST until November 2 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Heavy snow expected. Total snow accumulations 8 to 14\ninches. Winds gusting as high as 50 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Feet.\n\n* WHEN...From 5 PM this afternoon to 11 AM MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult, especially tonight and\nMonday morning over Wolf Creek Pass and Cumbres Pass. Strong winds\ncould produce areas of blowing and drifting snow.","ends":"2026-11-02T11:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.994b8191c6e7030d91cd62eb8345f4293ce0424b.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.994b8191c6e7030d91cd62eb8345f4293ce0424b.001.1"},{"event":"Avalanche Advisory","headline":"Avalanche Advisory issued October 31 at 7:16PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"SABCO\n\nTHE FOLLOWING MESSAGE IS TRANSMITTED AT THE REQUEST OF THE\nCOLORADO AVALANCHE INFORMATION CENTER.\n\n...A SPECIAL AVALANCHE ADVISORY IN EFFECT FROM 4:30 PM SATURDAY\nUNTIL 4:30 PM MONDAY...\n\n*WHAT...Avalanche conditions are dangerous above treeline.\n*WHERE...West Elk Mountains, Elk Mountains, San Juan Mountains, and\nLa Plata Mountains\n*WHEN...From 4:30 PM Saturday until 4:30 PM Monday.\n*IMPACTS...Backcountry travelers can easily trigger dangerous\navalanches large enough to bury a human.\n\n*PRECAUTION/PREPAREDNESS ACTIONS...A potent winter storm increases\navalanche danger Sunday into Monday. Rain, snow, and wind will cause\nnatural avalanches above treeline. Check the forecast at\nwww.colorado.gov/avalanche.\n\nBeyer & Pritchett","ends":"2026-11-02T16:30:00-07:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"West Elk and Sawatch Mountains; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5d9a0ec4f46df7deb3c2c0e5015df58147db243f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5d9a0ec4f46df7deb3c2c0e5015df58147db243f.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-01T21:22:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 012122 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 222 PM MST Sun Nov 1 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Heavy rainfall will continue across the ern San Juans into the evening, with significant and dangerous flooding expected from the mountains downstream into the western edge of the San Luis Valley. - Snow level finally drops late tonight, with several inches of snow","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-01T07:07:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 010707 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 107 AM MDT Sun Nov 1 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-020715- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mosqu","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},"fwf":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-01T07:05:00+00:00","snippet":".Discussion... No critical fire weather conditions are expected over the next several days. Despite strong winds around 3-50 mph today through Tuesday morning, humidity values will remain above critical fire weather thresholds. Otherwise, showers are expected today and through Monday, with snow around 10,000 plus feet, and rain below that. The heaviest precipitation is expected across the San Juan","url":"https://forecast.wea